@10100000 = ~Install Forest Warden - Fighter kit~ //Forest Warden: Install Kit Component
@10100001 = ~forest warden~ //Forest Warden: Lower Case Kit Name
@10100002 = ~Forest Warden~ //Forest Warden: Mixed Case Kit Name
@10100003 = ~FOREST WARDEN: By focusing on the arboreal aspects of the wild under the patronage of the Oak Father Silvanus, the Forest Warden has found <PRO_HIMHER>self surging with primal power. This power slowly transforms <PRO_HIMHER> into a sentient embodiment of nature.

Advantages:
– +1 bonus to Strength and Constitution.
– May use the Ingrain ability once per day. Gains one use at level 1.

INGRAIN: The Forest Warden regenerates 2 Hit Points (+2 every 2 levels) every round for 5 rounds. While regenerating the Forest Warden cannot move, has <PRO_HISHER> Dexterity halved, and gains a 25% penalty to Fire Resistance.

– May use the Spruce Strength ability once per day. Gains one use at level 4, and an additional use every 4 levels thereafter.

SPRUCE STRENGTH: For 1 turn the Forest Warden gains a 25% penalty to Fire Resistance and a 50% movement rate penalty. In exchange <PRO_HESHE> receives a +2 bonus to Armor Class, and all melee attacks made by the Forest Warden cause an additional 1d4 crushing damage plus 1 point per 2 levels to all enemies in a 10-ft. radius of the impact.

– May use the Snapthorns ability once per day. Gains one use at level 7 and an additional use every 7 levels thereafter.

SNAPTHORNS: The Forest Warden targets a point within 45 feet. For 1 turn all enemies in a 30-ft. radius of that point must are drawn towards it, and take 1d6 piercing and 1d6 slashing damage unless they make a Save vs. Breath.

Disadvantages:
– Alignment must have a neutral component.
– -2 Penalty to Dexterity.
– Gains a 35% weakness to fire.
– May only wear leather, studded leather, and hide armor.
– May not exceed High Mastery (four slots) in any weapon druids can use.
– May not exceed Proficiency (one slot) in any other weapon.~ //Forest Warden: Kit Description - Vanilla

@10100004 = ~Ingrain~ //Forest Warden: Ability 1 Name
@10100005 = ~Ingrain
The Forest Warden regenerates 2 Hit Points per 2 levels every round for 5 rounds. While regenerating the Forest Warden cannot move, has <PRO_HISHER> Dexterity halved, and gains a 25% penalty to Fire Resistance.~ //Forest Warden: Ability 1 Description
@10100006 = ~Rooted~ //Forest Warden: Ability 1 Effect Text

@10100007 = ~Spruce Strength~ //Forest Warden: Ability 2 Name
@10100008 = ~Spruce Strength
For 1 turn the Forest Warden gains a 25% penalty to Fire Resistance and a 50% movement rate penalty. In exchange <PRO_HESHE> receives a +2 bonus to Armor Class and Saving Throws, and all melee attacks made by the Forest Warden cause an additional 1d4 crushing damage (plus 1 point every 2 levels) to all enemies in a 10-ft. radius of the impact.~ //Forest Warden: Ability 2 Description
@10100009 = ~Forest Might~ //Forest Warden: Ability 2 Effect Text
@10100010 = ~~

@10100011 = ~Snapthorns~ //Forest Warden: Ability 3 Name
@10100012 = ~Snapthorns
The Forest Warden targets a point within 45 feet and for 1 turn all enemies in a 30-ft. radius of that point must are drawn towards it, and take 1d6 damage, unless they make a Save vs. Breath.~ //Forest Warden: Ability 3 Description
@10100013 = ~Vined~ //Forest Warden: Ability 3 Effect Text

@10100014 = ~Oakheart~ //Forest Warden: High Level Ability Name
@10100015 = ~Oakheart
The Forest Warden deepens <PRO_HISHER> connection to the natural world, turning further into a tree. Gains a base Armor Class of 5, an additional 50% weakness to fire, and a 20% resistance to Piercing damage. +2 bonus to Strength and Constitution, -4 penalty to Dexterity. The Forest Warden also cannot be affected by poison, entangling effects, and mind affecting effects.~ //Forest Warden: High Level Ability Description
@10100016 = ~Base Armor Class permanently changed to 5. Permanent additional 50% fire weakness, 20% Piercing resistance. Bonus +2 Strength and Constitution, -4 Dexterity. Immunity to Poison, Entangling effects, and Mind Affecting Effects~ //Forest Warden: High Level Ability Effect Text

