@50100000 = ~Install Trickster - Thief kit~ //Trickster: Install Kit Component
@50100001 = ~trickster~ //Trickster: Lower Case Kit Name
@50100002 = ~Trickster~ //Trickster: Mixed Case Kit Name
@50100003 = ~TRICKSTER~ //Trickster: Upper Case Kit Name
@50100004 = ~The Trickster may take formal study later in <PRO_HISHER> life but for now <PRO_HESHE> only dabbles in casting arcane magic. Coming at the cost of <PRO_HISHER> thieving abilities, the Trickster considers this a more then adequete price to pay for different opportunities for mischief.~ //Trickter: Kit Description
@50100005 = ~Advantages:
– Gains Arcane Tricks, giving the Trickster the ability to cast certain amount of Wizard spells per day. The amount of spells cast per day, and which spells able to be cast, are as follows.
 Level 1:
  Colour Spray, Friends, Magic Missile, Sleep, Spook
  Gains one use at level 1, and additional uses at levels 3, 5, and 7
 Level 2:
  Blur, Glitterdust, Invisibility, Luck, Mirror Image
  Gains one use at level 4, and additional uses at levels 6, 8, and 10
 Level 3:
  Dispel Magic, Haste, Non-Detection, Slow
  Gains one use at level 7, and additional uses at levels 9, 11, and 13
 Level 4:
  Confusion, Greater Malison, Improved Invisibility, Wizard Eye
  Gains one use at level 10, and additional uses at levels 12, 14, and 16
 Level 5:
  Domination, Lower Resistance, Shadow Door
  Gains one use at level 13, and additional uses at levels 15, 17, and 19

Disadvantages:
– Alignment restricted to non-lawful
– May only distribute 15 skill points per level (25 at level 1) among thieving skills.
– May not cast Tricks wearing studded leather armor or heavier.
– May not use Set Snare ability.
– -2 to backstab multiplier compared to an unkitted Thief:
  Level 1-8: x1 (no multiplier)
  Level 9-12: x2
  Level 13+: x3~ //Trickster: Kit Ability Block - Vanilla
@50100006 = ~Currently wearing Armor heavier than leather. Trick lost.~ //Trickster: Passive Effect Text
@50100007 = ~Arcane Trick: Level 1~ //Trickster: Ability 1 Name 
@50100008 = ~Arcane Trick: Level 1
The Trickster can cast one of the following Level 1 Wizard spells:
 Colour Spray
 Friends
 Magic Missile
 Sleep
 Spook~ //Trickster: Ability 1 Description - Vanilla
@50100009 = ~Arcane Trick: Level 2~ //Trickster: Ability 2 Name
@50100010 = ~Arcane Trick: Level 2
The Trickster can cast one of the following Level 2 Wizard spells:
 Blur
 Glitterdust
 Invisibility
 Luck
 Mirror Image~ //Trickster: Ability 2 Description - Vanilla
@50100011 = ~Arcane Trick: Level 3~ //Trickster: Ability 3 Name
@50100012 = ~Arcane Trick: Level 3
The Trickster can cast one of the following Level 3 Wizard spells:
 Dispel Magic
 Haste
 Non-Detection
 Slow~ //Trickster: Ability 3 Description - Vanilla
@50100013 = ~Arcane Trick: Level 4~ //Trickster: Ability 4 Name
@50100014 = ~Arcane Trick: Level 4
The Trickster can cast one of the following Level 4 Wizard spells:
 Confusion
 Greater Malison
 Improved Invisibility
 Wizard Eye~ //Trickster: Ability 4 Description - Vanilla
@50100015 = ~Arcane Trick: Level 5~ //Trickster: Ability 5 Name
@50100016 = ~Arcane Trick: Level 5
The Trickster can cast one of the following Level 5 Wizard spells:
 Domination
 Lower Resistances
 Shadow Door~ //Trickster: Ability 5 Description - Vanilla
@50100017 = ~Arcane Trick: Level 6~ //Trickster: High Level Ability Name
@50100018 = ~Arcane Trick: Level 6
Extensive familiarity with magic has given the Trickster the abiility to cast the following Level 6 Wizard Spells:
 Improved Haste
 Mislead
 Pierce Magic~ //Trickster: High Level Ability Description - Vanilla
 
