@50900000 = ~Install Seeker - Thief kit~ //Seeker: Install Kit Component
@50900001 = ~seeker~ //Seeker: Lower Case Kit Name
@50900002 = ~Seeker~ //Seeker: Mixed Case Kit Name
/*
   May cast Level 1 spells once per day. Gains one use at level 1, and additional uses at levels 3, 5, and 7 
   May cast Level 2 spells once per day. Gains one use at level 4, and additional uses at levels 6, 8, and 10
   May cast Level 3 spells once per day. Gains one use at level 7, and additional uses at levels 9, 11 and 13
   May cast Level 4 spells once per day. Gains one use at level 10, and additional uses at levels 12, 14, and 16
   May cast Level 5 spells once per day. Gains one use at level 13, and additional uses at levels 15, 17, and 19
*/
@50900003 = ~SEEKER~ //Seeker: Upper Case Kit Name
@50900004 = ~The Seeker has always heard the voices in <PRO_HISHER> ears but they were not the angry or sorrowful wails of the departed. Instead <PRO_HESHE> heard the murmurs of the trees, the breaths of animals, the songs of the land and sky. It is these that empower the Seeker and give <PRO_HIMHER> <PRO_HISHER> magic.~ //Seeker: Kit Description
@50900005 = ~Advantages:
– Gains Primal Whispers, giving the Seeker the ability to cast certain amount of Priest spells per day. The amount of spells cast per day, and which spells able to be cast, are as follows.
 Level 1:
  Bless, Doom, Entangle, Shillelagh, Spirit Ward
  Gains one use at level 1, and additional uses at levels 3, and 5
 Level 2:
  Barkskin, Charm Person or Mammal, Flame Blade, Goodberries, Writhing Fog
  Gains one use at level 4, and additional uses at levels 6, and 8
 Level 3:
  Call Lightning, Hold Animal, Spiritual Clarity, Summon Insects
  Gains one use at level 7, and additional uses at levels 9, and 11
 Level 4:
  Call Woodland Beings, Neutralize Poison, Poison, Spirit Fire
  Gains one use at level 10, and additional uses at levels 12, and 14
 Level 5:
  Ironskin, Pixie Dust, Recall Spirit
  Gains one use at level 13, and additional uses at levels 15, and 17

Disadvantages:
– Alignment must have a neutral component.
– May only distribute 20 skill points per level (30 at level 1) among thieving skills.
– Gains Set Snare ability uses later than a normal thief, with one use at level 1 and an additional use every 7 levels thereafter.
– -2 to backstab multiplier compared to an unkitted Thief:
  Level 1-8: x1 (no multiplier)
  Level 9-12: x2
  Level 13+: x3~ //Seeker: Kit Ability Block - Vanilla
@50900006 = ~Primal Whisper: Level 1~ //Seeker: Ability 1 Name
@50900007 = ~Primal Whisper: Level 1
The Seeker can cast one of the following Level 1 Priest Spells
 Bless
 Doom
 Entangle
 Shillelagh
 Spirit Ward~ //Seeker: Ability 1 Description - Vanilla
@50900008 = ~Primal Whisper: Level 2~ //Seeker: Ability 2 Name
@50900009 = ~Primal Whisper: Level 2
The Seeker can cast one of the following Level 2 Priest Spells
 Barkskin
 Charm Person or Mammal
 Flame Blade
 Goodberries
 Writhing Fog~ //Seeker: Ability 2 Description - Vanilla
@50900010 = ~Primal Whisper: Level 3~ //Seeker: Ability 3 Name
@50900011 = ~Primal Whisper: Level 3
The Seeker can cast one of the following Level 3 Priest Spells
 Call Lightning
 Hold Animal
 Spiritual Clarity
 Summon Insects~ //Seeker: Ability 3 Description - Vanilla
@50900012 = ~Primal Whisper: Level 4~ //Seeker: Ability 4 Name
@50900013 = ~Primal Whisper: Level 4
The Seeker can cast one of the following Level 4 Priest Spells
 Call Woodland Beings
 Neutralize Poison
 Poison
 Spirit Fire~ //Seeker: Ability 4 Description - Vanilla
@50900014 = ~Primal Whisper: Level 5~ //Seeker: Ability 5 Name
@50900015 = ~Primal Whisper: Level 5
The Seeker can cast one of the following Level 5 Priest Spells
 Ironskin
 Pixie Dust
 Recall Spirit~ //Seeker: Ability 5 Description - Vanilla
@50900016 = ~Primal Whisper: Level 6~ //Seeker: High Level Ability Name
@50900017 = ~Primal Whisper: Level 6
Attuning <PRO_HISHER> spirit closer to the primal world has given the Seeker the ability to cast the following Level 6 Priest Spells
 Conjure Animals
 Dolorous Decay
 Spiritual Lock~ //Seeker: High Level Ability Description - Vanilla
